Make Lockpicking account-wide, matching how Riding already works.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp, Spell::CanOpenLock()

Why: player request -- an alt with 0 Lockpicking should be able to open
anything a higher-Lockpicking character on the same account could, the
same way Riding is already account-wide in this module. The native
LOCK_KEY_SKILL check in CanOpenLock() only ever reads the casting
character's own GetSkillValue(skillId); this patch swaps that read for an
account-wide max (LivingGear_AccountLockpickSkill(), defined in
modules/mod-living-gear/src/LivingGear_Gather.cpp, reusing the same
AccountSkill() query already proven for gathering professions) but only
when skillId == SKILL_LOCKPICKING specifically -- every other
LOCK_KEY_SKILL type (Herbalism/Mining/Blasting/Disarm Trap/Inscription)
keeps the normal per-character check, since those gathering locks are
already handled entirely by Living Gear's own scan-based auto-gather
system and never need this path to begin with.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
@@ near the top, after the #include block
 #include <cmath>

+// Living Gear core-patch: makes Lockpicking account-wide (LivingGear_Gather.cpp).
+uint32 LivingGear_AccountLockpickSkill(Player* player);
+
@@ Spell::CanOpenLock(uint32 effIndex, uint32 lockId, SkillType& skillId, int32& reqSkillValue, int32& skillValue)
                         // castitem check: rogue using skeleton keys. the skill values should not be added in this case.
-                        skillValue = m_CastItem || !m_caster->IsPlayer() ?
-                                     0 : m_caster->ToPlayer()->GetSkillValue(skillId);
+                        skillValue = m_CastItem || !m_caster->IsPlayer() ? 0 :
+                                     skillId == SKILL_LOCKPICKING ? int32(LivingGear_AccountLockpickSkill(m_caster->ToPlayer())) :
+                                     m_caster->ToPlayer()->GetSkillValue(skillId);
